WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.968
-It seems like there's so much

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.002
going on right now.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.036
Today the House sent

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.472
the impeachment articles
to the Senate.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.608
A cheating scandal
in Major League Baseball

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.943
cost the Boston Red Sox
manager his job.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.179
[ Cheering and applause ]
Ken Jennings --

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.380
Ken Jennings won

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.248
the "Jeopardy!"
Greatest of All Time tournament.

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:19.018
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.721
And an entire town in Michigan
smells like weed

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.289
because so many residents
are growing it.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.258
[ Cheering, laughter,
and applause ]
There's a lot to go over,

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.093
so let's just jump in
and cover it all at once.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.161 line:0%
It is time for "News Smash."

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:34.199 line:0%
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:36.302
First up, impeachment.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.636
Today the house voted to send

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:39.838
the impeachment articles
over to the Senate.

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:42.007
There's no doubt that
President Trump is in trouble.

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:43.943
He put himself in serious

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.678
[ Laughter and cheering ]
"Jeopardy!" The tournament

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.447
was so fun to watch!

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.715
Ken Jennings made it look
easy up there.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.283
It was almost like he was

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:52.818
Cheating.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:55.721
Red Sox manager Alex Cora
organized a scheme

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.657
to steal signs from catchers.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.125
Now, he's out of a job.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.861
To cheer himself up, he might
have to take a little trip to

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.064
Weed Town, USA.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.932
The whole town
of Bessemer, Michigan,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.802
smells like weed 'cause so many
residents like to grow it.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.403
These people smoke so much weed,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.371
you bet you can never
see them on

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.140
"Jeopardy!" It was
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.141
a historic,
once-in-a-generation event

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:19.044
that we all got to watch on TV,
just like the

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:20.413
Impeachment.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.248
The trial starts soon
and there's new evidence

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.016
that Trump's associates
threatened people

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.618
to get dirt on Biden.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:28.654
Democrats are saying that's
not okay and totally

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.489
Stinks. This
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.959
town's changing Michigan from
Great Lakes State

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.395
to the Dank Stank State.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.997
Growing that much weed
is a bold move. It takes

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.100
Balls. The Red Sox
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.067
could see them coming
from a mile away,

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.736
since they knew the signs.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.037
But they got caught.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.339
They never should've

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.140
Wagered it all. And that's
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.275
what Ken Jennings did,
and it paid off big-time.

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:53.480
His score was so high, in fact,
he might as well live in

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.913
Bessemer, Michigan. So,
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:57.483
in conclusion, good luck,

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.785
good luck,

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.453
What is good luck?

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.122
[ Laughter ]
What is -- Wait, what?

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.256
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:07.427
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.233
-Acting!

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:15.401
-[Chuckle]

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.836
You guys,
I'm excited about this.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.838
Robert Downey Jr. is
my guest tonight!

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.975
[ Boisterous cheering
and applause ]

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.646
He stars in the new movie
"Dolittle."

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:29.748
Yep, "Dolittle,"
which pretty much sums up

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:31.117
last night's Democratic debate.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.552
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.787
That's right, last night was
the seventh Democratic debate

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.957
and a lot of people are saying
that it was pretty dull.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.925
It's odd, 'cause I really
thought six white people

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.927
standing behind podiums
onstage for two hours

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.129
was gonna be a rager!

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.397
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.864
But the main reason
people watched was

00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:48.334
to see Elizabeth Warren
and Bernie Sanders go at it

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.170
after Bernie
reportedly told her

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.804
a woman couldn't win
the presidency.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.606
-Ooh.
-At the end of the debate,

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.408
it seemed like there was
still some tension there.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.676
Check out what happened
when Bernie went

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.210
to shake Warren's hand.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.513
[ Applause ]
-The Democratic debate
in Des Moines, Iowa.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.415
This was the last time
Americans will hear

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.850
[ Laughter ]
the Democratic candidates all

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.818
onstage together.
Twenty days,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.486
six candidates onstage.
-Yeah, wow.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.889
-Laser focus on policy,
Iran, healthcare.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.090
-Can we see them again?

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.425
[ Laughter ]
-Ooh.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.327
-Bernie looks
like a Delta gate agent

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.929
who caught someone in zone 2
trying to board in zone 1.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.831
[ Laughter and applause ]
[gruffly] "There are rules!

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.766
There are rules, ma'am!

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.135
I'm gonna ask you."

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.469
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.837
That exchange looked
pretty intense.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.173
Luckily, we were able to get
the enhanced audio

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.641
-Ooh.
-of what they were saying.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.943
It seems like people might be
blowing this outta proportion.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.711
Check it out.
-[whispering] Hey, Bernie,

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:33.846
I was wondering if you've heard

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.448
Justin Bieber's new song
"Yummy."

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.815
-[whispering] What?
-It goes...

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:37.884
♪ You've got that
yummy, yummy ♪

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.418
-No! Listen!

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.621
The only Bieber song
I listen to is "Sorry."

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:42.621
-"Yummy's" better.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:43.856
-Your opinion, not mine.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.258
Agree to disagree.
-Hey, when you're talkin'

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.226
about the 1%,
are you talkin' about me?

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.227
-[Bleep] off.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.897
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.031
-Wow!

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.933
[ Cheering and applause ]
We got that audio.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.869
My goodness.
Wow!

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.704
-One of the biggest moments
from last night's debate

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:01.941
was Amy Klobuchar talking
about her election record.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.677
Check it out.
-My Republican opponents

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.213
have gotten
out of politics for good

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:11.217
[ Laughter ]
and I think -- I think
that sounds pretty goo-oo-d.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.218
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.620
-[as Klobuchar]
Pretty goo-oo-d!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.721
Pretty goo-oo-d.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:16.922
It was trending
on Twitter last night.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.290
[as Klobuchar] Pretty goo-oo-d.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.458
But I noticed you can
actually use

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:20.493
[as Klobuchar] pretty goo-oo-d

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.794
to describe a lot of things.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.529
Like, for example,
if you get an alert

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.198
that your Grubhub order
is arriving early, that's...

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:27.366
-Pretty goo-oo-d.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.001
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.036
If you send the wrong text,
but switch your phone

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:32.939
to airplane mode just
in time, that's...

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.840
-Pretty goo-oo-d.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.475
Or finally,
if you happen to stop by

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:38.444
Weed Town, USA, that's...

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.079
-[warbling slow-mo]
Pretty goo-oo-d.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.447
[ Laughter and applause ]
See? It works
in a bunch of ways.

00:04:42.447 --> 00:04:45.518
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:51.090
And, now that the Iowa caucuses
are just weeks away,

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.726
voters in the state are being
bombarded with campaign ads.

00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:56.829
The battle for airwaves
have gotten so intense

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.298
that Mike Bloomberg is now
attacking the MyPillow guy.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.033
-Wow.
[ Polite laughter ]

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.969
[ Laughing, claps ]

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.770
-We knew that joke wasn't
gonna work

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.305
about 20 minutes ago,
but we still --

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:07.539
[ Laughter ]
-Tried it, anyway, you know?

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:09.642
-We still wanted to try
and see if it worked.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.110
And it didn't.
-It did not.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.244
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:13.712
-I just like saying
MyPillow guy.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:14.781
-Come on. Who doesn't?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:16.515
-Even though he wasn't
at the debate,

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:19.651
Mike Bloomberg's campaign
tried gaining some attention

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:22.355
by tweeting out a bunch
of weird, absurd facts

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:23.689
that had nothing
to do with the election.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:24.823
Did anyone see this?

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.059
They even posted a photo
of Bloomberg's face

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.561
on a meatball.
Check this out.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.330
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.967
It says, "Spot the meatball
that looks like Mike."

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.802
So, if you're keeping track,
Bloomberg's appeared

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:39.038
in zero debates,
but on one meatball.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.472
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.441
Well, as I mentioned,
today the House finally voted

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:45.478
to send the articles
of impeachment to the Senate.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.113
I don't know, maybe it's
just me, but the impeachment

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:49.014
sort of feels like
"Grey's Anatomy."

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:50.615
Every time I see it,
my first thought is,

00:05:50.615 --> 00:05:51.984
"Is that still on TV?"

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.653
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.689
That's right, Pelosi appointed
seven impeachment managers,

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.325
who will prosecute the case
against Trump.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.326
I don't know if that
was a good idea.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.394
I mean, when you pick seven,

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:02.662
aren't you begging Trump
to give them

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:05.264
dwarf nicknames
from "Snow White"? It's like...

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.266
[as Trump] There's Congressman
Dopey, Sleepy, Grumpy."

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:11.370
Can we see a photo of Pelosi
and the seven managers?

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.305
-Yeah.
-I know it doesn't seem

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:15.007
like much, but, compared
to last night's debate,

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.709
that looks like the cast
of "Dolemite."

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:19.011
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.480
[ Applause ]

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:22.982
And maybe Pelosi was smart

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.417
to delay sending
over the articles

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.985
'cause there's new evidence
in the case against Trump.

00:06:26.985 --> 00:06:29.388
It turns out that one
of Rudy Giuliani's associates,

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:32.258
Lev Parnas, actually wrote
a note that said,

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:34.026
"get Zalensky to
Announce that

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.395
the Biden case
will Be Investigated."

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:37.796
Trump was furious.
He was like...

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:38.798
[as Trump]
You stayed at the Ritz,

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:39.899
instead of one of my hotels?

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:43.568
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.568 --> 00:06:44.703
But Trump's keeping busy.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.372
Last night he held
a rally in Wisconsin,

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.774
where he ranted
about dishwashers.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.777
He said people have to run them
ten times to get things clean.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:53.613
[ Laughter ]
First of all, since when

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:54.747
does Trump use a dishwasher?

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.048
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.483
Everything he eats comes
in a wrapper.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.851
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.754
Second, Trump said the same
exact thing about toilets.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.956
Yeah. He said people
are flushing toilets ten times

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.425
to get them to work.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.625
I think I know
what's going on here.

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:08.461
I think Trump's washing
his dishes in the toilet

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.328
and he's going to the bathroom
in the dishwasher.

00:07:10.328 --> 00:07:11.364
[ Ewwing and ohhing ]

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:13.266
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:14.900
During an event today,
Trump welcomed

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.435
several business leaders
to the White House,

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:20.139
including Ford executive
Nancy Joy Falotico.
["Fallateeko"]

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.474
Let's see how that went.

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:24.477
-Nancy Fallohtohco, of Ford.

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:25.977
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.977 --> 00:07:27.846
Nancy, where are you?

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:30.816
-[as Trump] Please welcome Nancy
from Ford versus Ferrari.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.552
[ Laughter ]
Some TV news:

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:35.655
"Jeopardy!'s" Greatest of All
Time tournament is over

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.923
and, in the end,
Ken Jennings won three games,

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:40.092
James Holzhauer won one,

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.861
and Brad Rutter didn't win any.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.929
Yep, Rutter's one
of "Jeopardy!'s" all-time greats

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:46.165
and, now, everyone looks
at him like, "Pfew, idiot!"

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.802
You guys, a lot of people
follow the news

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:52.070
by just checking out
what's trending on Twitter,

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.806
but sometimes seeing
just a hashtag

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:56.241
doesn't tell the whole story,
so, to quickly catch you up

00:07:56.241 --> 00:07:57.943
on the week,
let's look at why some

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.378
of these things were trending.

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.347
First up, there's the
#incoherentdisaster.

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:04.350
You may think it's trending
because Trump ranting

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.718
about toilets at his rally,

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:07.386
[ Laughter ]
but #incoherentdisaster is

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.688
